# A lens constraining the field it takes with a default: it must be _, and what the lens copies is the defaulted disjunction, not a value.
-- source.cue --
b: string
-- target.cue --
a: string
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: {b: *"d" | string}
v1_0: {a: v0_0.b}
-- out --
not total
v0_0 is {b: *"d" | string}, a constraint on what the lens receives; v0_0 must be _, so that the source schema alone says what the lens takes (rule source-constrained) @ lens.cue:1:1
v1_0.a is *"d" | string, a disjunction rather than a value; a result field must have one concrete value (rule not-a-value) @ lens.cue:2:11
